<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut due high winds.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut due high winds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Black Sea port of Novorossiisk was closed early on Wednesday morning because of bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port, which is the main outlet for Russian Urals crude oil to southern European refineries, closed at 0430 (local time) on Wednesday because of high winds and thunderstorms, the sources said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk was also closed between 2115 (local time) on Monday and 1945 (local time) on Tuesday, the source added.</p>
<p>Three vessels were alongside on Wednesday, two waiting to load crude oil and one fuel oil.</p>
<p>A further five crude tankers were at anchor, the source added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
